  "result": "`slugify` is now implemented in `src/strings.js`, and `npm test` passes all 12 tests (the 2 existing ones plus 10 new).\n\n- **How it works:** It maps `đ`/`Đ` to `d`, strips diacritics, lowercases, and turns every run of non-`a-z0-9` characters into one hyphen. It then trims the leading hyphen, cuts to 50 characters, and trims any trailing hyphen left by the cut.\n- **New tests** (in `test/strings.test.js`): they cover:\n  - lowercasing and hyphenating\n  - Vietnamese diacritics\n  - `đ`/`Đ`\n  - other Latin accents\n  - collapsing runs of symbols\n  - trimming hyphens at both ends\n  - input with nothing usable (returns `''`)\n  - the 50-character cut\n  - a cut that lands on a hyphen\n  - a slug of exactly 50 characters\n\nOne of my new tests failed on the first run because I miscounted its input (49 a's plus `-b` is 51 characters). The implementation was right, so I corrected the test.",
